E226 Amendment 1 start; 75 items; settings Config(row=1, ranking=0, control_size=0.1, control_site=0); thresholds {'control_tol': 1e-05, 'R_repro_tol': 1e-05, 'ratio_min': 1e-12, 'split_fp64_tol': 1e-12, 'F_from_pieces_tol': 0.0001, 'M_from_pieces_tol': 0.0001, 'thresholds_source': "ratio_min: 1 - s_u is computed in fp64 as 1 - cos^2 with cos^2 near 1, so its absolute error is ~1e-16 (fp64 unit roundoff); a part with ratio_u under 1e-12 would carry an error in t_u of 1e-4 or more, and a known item's split puts a tiny change on every subcomponent of its site (n_changed 3,585 for x10, experiments/kstar_vpd/results/items/x10.json), so such parts are left out of N and counted (n_small) rather than let rounding set t; split_fp64_tol, F_from_pieces_tol, M_from_pieces_tol: E226's filed values (experiments/kstar_vpd/results/predictions.json), the same split; control_tol: the construction identities hold to fp64 rounding (~1e-15) once the pieces are fp32 (|du|^2 / |u|^2 and u . du then off by ~1e-7 relative), so 1e-5 relative catches a formula error (order 1) and not rounding; R_repro_tol: R recomputed on E226's saved K* with the fp64 s against R from E226's saved fp32 s, a guard that the item rebuilt is the one E226 read: the smallest R difference between two known items is 3e-4 (x2 0.99921, moved 0.99889, experiments/r_reanalysis/results/summary.json .known.R.values), and 1e-5 is 30x under it; a GPU other than E226's H100 changes the fp32 forwards by reduction order only (~1e-7 relative), and the first item logs its deviation"}
